<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benjamin D'Urban</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1777–1849</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Benjamin D'Urban</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Benjamin D'Urban was a British army officer and governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> from 1834 to 1838. After the Sixth Xhosa War he annexed the land between the Keiskamma and Kei rivers in 1835 as the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-saxe-meiningen">Queen Adelaide</a>, but the British government reversed the annexation in 1836. The city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durban">Durban</a> is named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benjamin-durban.jpg" alt="Benjamin D'Urban" width="300" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Benjamin_d%27Urban_(1777-1849).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
